    "Documented cross-voice MusicXML tie route in P3, measure 88: The original viola bar 88 encodes simultaneous identical dotted-half A4 notes in voices 1 and 4 at q261; only voice 4 carries the outgoing tie, while bar 89’s first A4 at q264 carries its stop in voice 1. Route only that explicit tie start onto the identical voice-1 unison so the written continuation ends at q265 without an invented reattack at q264. Preserve both original notes, their onsets and durations, and the voice-4 inverted fermata; change only tie ownership in a disposable derivative.",
    "Native-source-backed trill span in P1, source quarters 25–28: Native violin-I trill ends at II.10 quarter 1, where the next trill starts. The MusicXML stop is at the end of a hidden voice-4 cue; retain the hidden cue and route only its ornament stop to the existing voice-1 onset.",
    "Native-source-backed trill span in P1, source quarters 28–31: Native violin-I trill ends at II.11 quarter 1, where the next trill starts. The MusicXML stop is at the end of a hidden voice-4 cue; preserve that cue's visibility and all timed notes.",
    "Native-source-backed trill span in P1, source quarters 31–36: Native violin-I next-location advances two measures minus one quarter from II.11 quarter 1, ending at II.13 quarter 0. The original stop belongs to the end of the hidden voice-3 rest in II.12, not its onset.",
    "Native-source-backed trill span in P1, source quarters 147–153: Native violin-I trill spans II.50–51 and ends at II.52 quarter 0. Preserve the hidden voice-3 rest carrying the exported stop and route only that stop to its source-defined ending in voice 1.",
    "Native-source-backed trill span in P1, source quarters 483.5–489: Native violin-I trill starts at II.160 quarter 0.5 and ends two measures minus half a quarter later, at II.162 quarter 0. The voice-2 rest's exported stop is an end-of-rest position, not an attack or a duration change.",
    "Native-source-backed trill span in P3, source quarters 528–530: Native viola E-flat5 trill lasts half a whole-note unit, ending at II.175 quarter 2 as the D5 trill begins. Keep the hidden voice-2 rest and place only its stop at the existing voice-1 D5 onset.",
